            5\n tcpkeepalive         1\n disksleep            10\n", "thermal": "Note: No thermal warning level has been recorded\nNote: No performance warning level has been recorded\nNote: No CPU power status has been recorded\n"}, "status": "completed", "attempts": [{"experiment_id": "a_transpose", "status": "failed", "error_type": "TimeoutExpired"}, {"experiment_id": "scratch_lifetime", "status": "abstained", "reason": "The selected experiment conflicts with its preservation requirements. Both existing K loops advance scratch by 256 bytes per K step and rewind 131072 bytes. The first 32-row tile alone accesses through scratch byte 130943, so reducing allocation to 65536 bytes without changing consumption would exceed bounds. The current traversal computes both 32-row halves for each B panel before advancing that panel. Computing all B panels for the first half before repacking the second half changes that traversal. A working 64 KiB design therefore requires changes to scratch stride, rewinds, second-half addressing, and compute traversal outside the permitted allocation/packing block. I cannot implement all stated requirements together or substitute a different experiment. No source changes or tests were performed."}, {"experiment_id": "sme_fp32_schedule", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-k-loop-counter-schedule", "hypothesis": "Moving the counter decrement before the four FMOPA instructions may reduce exposed loop-control latency. This implements only the selected scheduling change in Llibxsmm_478 and Llibxsmm_70c. Each loop retains 512 iterations, the same loads and pointer updates, unchanged FP32 accumulation order, and the branch after all four FMOPA operations. The supplied history contains no identical change. All other code, including the complete BSD notice, packing, ABI, streaming transitions and general-size fallback, remains unchanged. Assembly, correctness and performance are untested. Validation requires the fixed compiler flags, 0.002 tolerance, general-size and boundary checks, and fresh repeated paired controls on unchanged battery power and settings. No speedup is established.", "source_hash": "71c55f82b9955eefda8ca17f47e59fbe04c98919c7d30d110a6c540f38005bb8"}, {"experiment_id": "register_reuse", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-k-loop-consume-before-pointer-updates", "hypothesis": "Both supplied K loops have the same instruction order. Move their two pointer updates after the four FMOPA operations so computation immediately follows the operand loads. Preserve the paired loads, registers, FMOPA order, counter and 512 iterations. Under the wrapper's operand swap, z0/z1 contain B values and z2/z3 contain packed A values. This distinct scheduling change tests earlier operand consumption; no gain is established. All other code and the complete BSD notice remain unchanged. Assembly, correctness and performance are untested. Validation requires the fixed flags, 0.002 tolerance, general-size and boundary checks, and fresh repeated paired controls with power source and settings unchanged.", "source_hash": "13bc6a2ba0dc662d722b0ba8d09db1f2fc55ef77396b1056243d5fb154bf3cdc"}, {"experiment_id": "sme_fp32_schedule", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-k-loop-interleaved-pointer-updates", "hypothesis": "Interleaving pointer updates with FMOPA operations tests whether their scheduling improves throughput. In both K loops, move the x0 update after the first FMOPA and the x3 update after the third. Loads, FP32 accumulation order, counter placement, 512 iterations and pointer strides remain unchanged. This schedule differs from the supplied prior candidates. All other code, including the complete BSD notice, packing, ABI, streaming transitions and general-size fallback, remains unchanged. Assembly, correctness and performance are untested; no gain is established. Validation requires the fixed compiler flags, 0.002 tolerance, n=512 and general-size boundary checks, followed by fresh repeated paired controls with power source and settings unchanged under the existing promotion rules.", "source_hash": "a748475df6036ec229169ae103e91d567ca0854e45d885c5c8887c2e9580c36a"}, {"experiment_id": "sme_fp32_tiles", "status": "failed", "error_type": "TimeoutExpired"}], "trials": [{"name": "libxsmm-aot-reference", "hypothesis": "Pinned LIBXSMM SME reference adapted to the frozen row-major beta-zero ABI", "source_hash": "7e9ab1076777a40cb0ad30527e381b221d4024cd99f370708971fb652b31810e", "status": "passed", "scores": [807.120791422058, 1035.7664763501227, 1076.972778471826], "control_scores": [], "promoted": null, "adjudication": null}, {"name": "libxsmm-k-loop-counter-schedule", "hypothesis": "Moving the counter decrement before the four FMOPA instructions may reduce exposed loop-control latency. This implements only the selected scheduling change in Llibxsmm_478 and Llibxsmm_70c. Each loop retains 512 iterations, the same loads and pointer updates, unchanged FP32 accumulation order, and the branch after all four FMOPA operations. The supplied history contains no identical change. All other code, including the complete BSD notice, packing, ABI, streaming transitions and general-size fallback, remains unchanged. Assembly, correctness and performance are untested. Validation requires the fixed compiler flags, 0.002 tolerance, general-size and boundary checks, and fresh repeated paired controls on unchanged battery power and settings. No speedup is established.", "source_hash": "71c55f82b9955eefda8ca17f47e59fbe04c98919c7d30d110a6c540f38005bb8", "status": "passed", "scores": [1052.6880968473677, 1015.5199985790974, 855.9121710529221], "control_scores": [866.5021857187708, 1093.0494478390983, 1087.1485421776142], "promoted": false, "adjudication": {"decision": "revise", "reason": "Recorded validation passed, but eligible=false prohibits adoption. Candidate scores were 855.9\u20131052.7 GFLOP/s versus paired controls of 866.5\u20131093.0. Paired changes were +21.5%, \u22127.1%, and \u221221.