constant bounds, transpose, or implementation choice."}}, {"name": "libxsmm-full512-padded-272-byte-a-slices", "hypothesis": "Implement the selected padding experiment in the full512 kernel: allocate 139264 bytes, pack 512 slices at 272-byte intervals, and update both packed-A consumer strides and rewinds. Each slice contains 256 data bytes followed by 16 unused bytes. The second row half still starts at byte 128; the final data byte is at offset 139247, within the allocation. B and C addressing, FP32 FMOPA order, one kernel call, SME transitions, general-size fallback, and both complete license notices remain unchanged. This corrected layout is absent from the supplied measured history. The hypothesis is that padding changes scratch cache mapping; cache geometry and benefit are unverified. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, full-GEMM correctness, and performance require fresh validation under the fixed gates and repeated paired controls with battery power and settings unchanged. No gain or throughput above 1800 GFLOP/s is established.", "source_hash": "0e428f343d60f7adb08f3627e633c382df52ec6417375aeeff58cc18c9916dca", "status": "passed", "scores": [1252.907603299889, 1252.907603299889, 1377.185282533294], "control_scores": [1132.4383837853318, 1549.7777397605503, 1441.2641417233476], "promoted": false, "adjudication": {"decision": "reject", "reason": "The fixed evaluator marked this candidate ineligible. Recorded correctness passed, but fresh Automatic battery paired differences were +10.6%, \u221219.2%, and \u22124.4%. Candidate throughput ranged from 1252.9\u20131377.2 GFLOP/s; controls ranged from 1132.4\u20131549.8. This variation and two losing pairs do not establish a repeatable gain over the imported LIBXSMM reference. No held-out result is supplied. Discard this candidate and retain the incumbent. These scores do not establish a cache-mapping cause or a power-mode kernel speedup."}}]}, {"phase": "cpu-libxsmm-next-board-2026-09-25", "calls": 73, "implementations": 6, "profile": {"cpu": "Apple M4 Pro", "power": "Battery Power", "streaming_fp32_lanes": 16, "capabilities": ["cpu", "arm64", "sme", "sme2", "neon", "simd", "single-thread"], "sme2": true, "p_core_l1d_bytes": 131072, "e_core_l1d_bytes": 65536, "cache_line_bytes": 128}, "host": {"timestamp_utc": "2026-09-25T09:58:39.411402+00:00", "battery": "Now drawing from 'Battery Power'\n -InternalBattery-0 (id=21889123)\t35%; discharging; 1:33 remaining present: true\n", "power_settings": "Battery Power:\n powermode            1\n Sleep On Power Button 1\n standby              1\n ttyskeepawake        1\n hibernatemode        3\n powernap             0\n hibernatefile        /var/vm/sleepimage\n displaysleep         10\n womp                 0\n networkoversleep     0\n sleep                3\n tcpkeepalive         1\n lessbright           1\n disksleep            10\nAC Power:\n Sleep On Power Button 1\n powermode            0\n standby              1\n ttyskeepawake        1\n hibernatemode        3\n powernap             1\n hibernatefile        /var/vm/sleepimage\n displaysleep         10\n womp                 1\n networkoversleep     0\n sleep                5\n tcpkeepalive         1\n disksleep            10\n", "thermal": "Note: No thermal warning level has been recorded\nNote: No performance warning level has been recorded\nNote: No CPU power status has been recorded\n"}, "status": "completed", "attempts": [{"experiment_id": "za_four_tile_reuse", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-full512-row-half-first-traversal", "hypothesis": "Change traversal within each packed 64-row band: compute the first 32 output rows across all sixteen column panels, then compute the second 32 rows across all sixteen panels. Keeping one packed row half active across a complete column sweep may improve reuse; this is unverified. At 16 FP32 lanes, four ZA.S tiles form one 32x32 output block. Both K loops, FMOPA order, stores, 256-byte scratch stride, 128 KiB allocation and SME transitions remain unchanged. After each sweep, reset B by 2048 bytes and advance C by 63488 bytes from its post-sweep position. The second half uses scratch base+128. These offsets cover each output block once and preserve the next 64-row band's starting pointers. General sizes, tails, n<=0, the unused helper and both complete license notices remain unchanged. This traversal is absent from the supplied measured history. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, full-GEMM correctness and performance remain untested; throughput above 1800 GFLOP/s is not established. Use the unchanged base source for fresh paired controls under the fixed gates and unchanged power settings.", "source_hash": "367df33b6712e12a758295c494b013fdd2f5aaa034bf82488cf8754f349a82a0"}, {"experiment_id": "b_panel_layout", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-full512-packed-b-column-panels", "hypothesis": "Pack B inside gemm as packed_b[p*16384+k*32+c] = B[k*512+p*32+c], for p=0..15, k=0..511 and c=0..31. Each panel occupies 65536 bytes; all sixteen occupy 1048576 bytes. Both K loops read two 16-lane FP32 vectors per step, advance B by 128 bytes, and rewind by 65536 bytes. Each column-panel transition advances by 65536 bytes; each completed column sweep rewinds by 1048576 bytes. Contiguous B access may offset the added packing and allocation cost; this is unverified. The original 64-row traversal, A packing, FP32 FMOPA order, C stores, single SME call, general-size fallback and both complete license notices remain unchanged. Allocation failure uses the existing fallback. This source change is distinct from the supplied measured inventory. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, full-GEMM correctness at tolerance 0.002, and fresh repeated paired performance gates remain required with power source and settings unchanged. No speedup or throughput above 1800 GFLOP/s is established.", "source_hash": "f21047135d3ab2f71b92c91cfca9546b101d4382563330f4bb375b2f94557a36"}, {"experiment_id": "loop_order", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-full512-column-panel-first-traversal", "hypothesis": "Interchange the full512 traversal: sixteen 32-column panels become the outer loop, with eight 64-row blocks inside each panel. Both 32-row halves stay together. Each row block packs its current A rows before both consumers, then advances A and C by 131072 bytes. After eight blocks, rewind A and C by 1048576 bytes and advance B and C by 128 bytes for the next column panel. B remains at the current panel throughout the row sweep. This tests B-panel reuse while increasing A packing from eight to 128 packs per GEMM; benefit is unverified. This differs from the measured row-half-first traversal and packed-B layout. The 512-step reductions, FP32 order, scratch layout, SME transitions, general-size fallback, n<=0 behavior, unused helper and both complete license notices remain unchanged. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, full-GEMM correctness and fresh repeated paired performance checks remain required under the unchanged gates and initial power settings. No speedup or throughput above 1800 GFLOP/s is established.", "source_hash": "7562203ea8753326f7d10004d50674912e8791c7f78ed90798d8c9e0a468ba0b"}, {"experiment_id": "prefetch_locality", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-full512-distance4-bounded-prefetch", "hypothesis": "Add guarded distance-4 prefetches in Llibxsmm_478 and Llibxsmm_70c. The supplied source advances B by 2048 bytes per K step, not the recommendation's 512 bytes; packed A advances by 256 bytes. Prefetch offsets are therefore 8192 and 1024 bytes. Prefetch only when x8>4, covering future K indices 4 through 511 without crossing the current panel or scratch allocation. Demand loads, pointer updates, FP32 FMOPA order, iteration counts, traversal, SME transitions, fallback and both complete license notices remain unchanged. This tests software prefetching and is distinct from the supplied measured sources. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, full-GEMM correctness and fresh paired performance gates remain required under the fixed contract and unchanged initial power settings. No speedup or throughput above 1800 GFLOP/s is established.", "source_hash": "9d1ad9bdbad475271fed38ce4dc70ae966892f5337d93fba28b183b33984fd65"}, {"experiment_id": "panel_packing", "status": "failed", "error_type": "TimeoutExpired"}, {"experiment_id": "address_generation", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-k-loop-joint-two-stream-end-tests", "hypothesis": "Replace the countdown in Llibxsmm_478 and Llibxsmm_70c with joint two-stream termination checks. Caller-saved x4 and x5 hold the initial B pointer plus 1048576 bytes and packed-A pointer plus 131072 bytes. CMP and conditional CCMP continue only while both pointers differ from their ends. With the unchanged strides, both reach their ends after exactly 512 ordered FP32 updates, including the second row half. No additional demand loads occur. This implements the selected joint check, distinct from the historical separate single-stream checks. It does not establish reduced instruction cost or a speedup. Pointer rewinds, traversal, packing, SME transitions, general-size fallback, n<=0 behavior, unused helper and both complete license notices remain unchanged. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, full-GEMM correctness and fresh repeated paired performance validation remain required under the unchanged gates and initial power settings. Throughput above 1800 GFLOP/s is not established.", "source_hash": "ef09f2a1067deb0c1160bb51dbc29457b071ef0e071ce04e01bfd586afd1dc97"}], "trials": [{"name": "libxsmm-reference-with-unused-panel32", "hypothesis": "Original full512 GEMM body plus an optional unused generated panel primitive", "source_hash": "e7b5eb8a9b290651137639917a3bdca342e9a1ed767d0ff8718449b03214c200", "status": "passed", "scores": [1078.2315304307879, 1013.5989131043257, 826.6954437505], "control_scores": [], "promoted": null, "adjudication": null}, {"name": "libxsmm-full512-row-half-first-