 GFLOP/s. Discard this candidate and retain the unchanged incumbent. These measurements do not isolate prefetch, guard-branch, or cache effects. Any future variant requires a distinct source change and fresh validation under the unchanged gates."}}, {"name": "libxsmm-k-loop-joint-two-stream-end-tests", "hypothesis": "Replace the countdown in Llibxsmm_478 and Llibxsmm_70c with joint two-stream termination checks. Caller-saved x4 and x5 hold the initial B pointer plus 1048576 bytes and packed-A pointer plus 131072 bytes. CMP and conditional CCMP continue only while both pointers differ from their ends. With the unchanged strides, both reach their ends after exactly 512 ordered FP32 updates, including the second row half. No additional demand loads occur. This implements the selected joint check, distinct from the historical separate single-stream checks. It does not establish reduced instruction cost or a speedup. Pointer rewinds, traversal, packing, SME transitions, general-size fallback, n<=0 behavior, unused helper and both complete license notices remain unchanged. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, full-GEMM correctness and fresh repeated paired performance validation remain required under the unchanged gates and initial power settings. Throughput above 1800 GFLOP/s is not established.", "source_hash": "ef09f2a1067deb0c1160bb51dbc29457b071ef0e071ce04e01bfd586afd1dc97", "status": "passed", "scores": [1048.7480498774569, 949.9349024586878, 1105.9971558990512], "control_scores": [1020.830164625027, 1064.1643453045485, 839.0784298226062], "promoted": false, "adjudication": {"decision": "revise", "reason": "Recorded correctness passed, but eligible=false prohibits adoption; promoted=false confirms no promotion. Candidate throughput was 949.9\u20131106.0 GFLOP/s versus paired controls of 839.1\u20131064.2. Paired changes were +2.7%, \u221210.7%, and +31.8%; candidate and control repeat spreads were 156.1 and 225.1 GFLOP/s. These mixed, variable results establish no repeatable gain or causal explanation. No repeat exceeded 1800 GFLOP/s. Retain the unchanged incumbent and treat joint pointer-end checks as unproven. The next implementation must use a distinct source change and hypothesis, with fresh paired validation under the unchanged gates and separate power-mode records."}}]}, {"phase": "cpu-libxsmm-editable-panel-2026-09-25", "calls": 72, "implementations": 6, "profile": {"cpu": "Apple M4 Pro", "power": "Battery Power", "streaming_fp32_lanes": 16, "capabilities": ["cpu", "arm64", "sme", "sme2", "neon", "simd", "single-thread"], "sme2": true, "p_core_l1d_bytes": 131072, "e_core_l1d_bytes": 65536, "cache_line_bytes": 128}, "host": {"timestamp_utc": "2026-09-25T18:37:16.299741+00:00", "battery": "Now drawing from 'Battery Power'\n -InternalBattery-0 (id=21889123)\t19%; discharging; 0:42 remaining present: true\n", "power_settings": "Battery Power:\n powermode            1\n Sleep On Power Button 1\n standby              1\n ttyskeepawake        1\n hibernatemode        3\n powernap             0\n hibernatefile        /var/vm/sleepimage\n displaysleep         10\n womp                 0\n networkoversleep     0\n sleep                3\n tcpkeepalive         1\n lessbright           1\n disksleep            10\nAC Power:\n Sleep On Power Button 1\n powermode            0\n standby              1\n ttyskeepawake        1\n hibernatemode        3\n powernap             1\n hibernatefile        /var/vm/sleepimage\n displaysleep         10\n womp                 1\n networkoversleep     0\n sleep                5\n tcpkeepalive         1\n disksleep            10\n", "thermal": "Note: No thermal warning level has been recorded\nNote: No performance warning level has been recorded\nNote: No CPU power status has been recorded\n"}, "status": "completed", "attempts": [{"experiment_id": "streaming_region_cost", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-n512-panel32-one-streaming-region", "hypothesis": "Reuse the panel32 packing and compute body for sixteen row panels inside one SME region with one 64 KiB scratch allocation. Saved registers x21/x22/x23 retain B/A/C bases, x26 retains scratch, x27 counts panels, and x28 holds the byte offset; these registers are saved and restored by the existing prologue and epilogue and are otherwise unused by the supplied helper body. Each panel resets B, A, C, scratch and the packing cursor. A and C advance by 65536 bytes, covering all 512 output rows once. SP resets to scratch after packing and returns to the saved stack top after the last panel. The FP32 K loop, ZA setup, output stores, general-size fallback and complete license notices remain unchanged. This differs from the measured sixteen-call wrapper. Reduced entry/exit overhead is an unverified hypothesis; comparison against full512 measures the complete layout and control-flow change and cannot isolate transition costs. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, full-GEMM correctness and fresh repeated paired performance validation remain required under the unchanged gates and initial power settings. No speedup or throughput above 1800 GFLOP/s is established.", "source_hash": "eb091b1eca431f0760d0d61e4c0c6e748c1a9e34466a87ac15ad9cb238b5aecf"}, {"experiment_id": "cache_blocking", "status": "abstained", "reason": "The selected experiment already exists as libxsmm-n512-panel32-one-streaming-region, source hash eb091b1eca431f0760d0d61e4c0c6e748c1a9e34466a87ac15ad9cb238b5aecf. Its supplied source implements sixteen row panels with one SME entry/exit, one 64 KiB scratch allocation, saved input bases, per-panel pointer resets, and unchanged K loops and stores. Correctness passed, but candidate scores of 998.4\u20131097.5 GFLOP/s versus paired controls of 964.0\u20131110.8 established no repeatable gain; it was not promoted. No repeat exceeded 1800 GFLOP/s. The selected proposal adds no distinct source change. Stop to avoid repeating the measured experiment."}, {"experiment_id": "n512_fast_path", "status": "absta