atch once. The legacy 1800 target flag does not determine this decision."}}, {"name": "libxsmm-full512-w32-k-loop-counters", "hypothesis": "Change only the counter initialization, decrement and branch in Llibxsmm_478 and Llibxsmm_70c from X8 to W8. Each loop retains exactly 512 iterations, the original loads, pointer increments, four ordered FP32 FMOPA operations and pointer rewinds. This tests 32-bit loop control; performance is unknown. This change is absent from the supplied measured inventory. ABI, general-size fallback, tails, n<=0 behavior and complete license notices remain unchanged. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, full-GEMM correctness at tolerance 0.002 and fresh repeated paired measurements remain required under the fixed gates and unchanged power settings. Throughput above 1800 GFLOP/s is not established.", "source_hash": "872c239816f8707fe5fa1b499c2e0455b625c6a4269f2944273f79d437b7bf92", "status": "passed", "scores": [1114.8022356612066, 1475.593029020843, 1525.5568912933259, 1667.7257078606644, 1050.628026141138, 1371.8994674387113, 1145.7303993633925, 1501.3840054854995, 1236.5567963778612, 1503.4947608597197], "control_scores": [1623.6048571085166, 1149.001470651942, 1555.390186319691, 1147.3659586351357, 1189.9631996958801, 1343.8571481748947, 1565.221352344687, 1307.578729510155, 1385.1730344217722, 1517.6562193759476], "promoted": false, "adjudication": {"decision": "reject", "reason": "Reported correctness passed, but eligible=false and promoted=false. Across ten fresh runs, candidate scores ranged from 1050.63\u20131667.73 GFLOP/s; paired controls ranged from 1147.37\u20131623.60. These ranges overlap, failing the fixed separated-ranges-plus-5% gate. The candidate won only 4/10 pairs. It exceeded neither the historical Battery Automatic peak of 1668.5964 nor the fresh AC Automatic baseline peak of 1685.6231: 0/10 runs for both. The ten-run consistency goal is unmet under either comparison; the peak definition remains pending. Discard this candidate and retain the incumbent. These measurements establish no causal benefit from W32 loop counters. The legacy 1800 target flag does not determine this decision."}}, {"name": "libxsmm-full512-fmopa-order-0132", "hypothesis": "Swap the ZA2 and ZA3 FMOPA instructions in Llibxsmm_478 and Llibxsmm_70c to test issue order 0,1,3,2. Each tile retains its operands, predicates and K=0..511 accumulation order. Loads, pointer updates, counters, rewinds, stores, fallback, ABI and complete license notices remain unchanged. This exact change is absent from the supplied measured history. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, full-GEMM correctness at tolerance 0.002 and fresh repeated paired performance checks remain required under the unchanged gates and initial power settings. No speedup, tile-reuse cause or throughput above 1800 GFLOP/s is established.", "source_hash": "1a81c422b6b62a1d60b4476417f224565e74849d402d4d54c09692b559dfa264", "status": "passed", "scores": [1660.0011098962214, 1638.8802183524394, 1492.6847216869094, 1462.863518238312, 1213.9533906839156, 1669.4680736575833, 1197.036566526102, 1455.921177408793, 1331.6307641877493, 1431.6557528888889], "control_scores": [1493.3822240207676, 1597.8301079223356, 1379.8399846410205, 1414.6796871134482, 1065.5752368657265, 1588.3754202583964, 1564.455013785286, 1160.3805030039377, 1635.9735844033382, 1509.8370826361868], "promoted": false, "adjudication": {"decision": "reject", "reason": "Reported correctness passed, but eligible=false and promoted=false. Across ten fresh AC Automatic runs, candidate scores ranged from 1197.04\u20131669.47 GFLOP/s; paired controls ranged from 1065.58\u20131635.97. These ranges overlap, failing the fixed separated-ranges-plus-5% gate. The candidate won 7/10 pairs, which does not establish a consistent gain. It exceeded the historical Battery Automatic peak of 1668.5964 in 1/10 runs and the fresh AC Automatic baseline peak of 1685.6231 in 0/10 runs. The ten-run goal is unmet under both comparisons; the peak definition remains pending. Discard this candidate and retain the incumbent. These measurements establish no causal benefit from the FMOPA order change. The legacy 1800 target flag does not determine this decision."}}]}, {"phase": "cpu-libxsmm-transpose-swarm-2026-09-25", "calls": 83, "implementations": 4, "profile": {"cpu": "Apple M4 Pro", "power": "AC Power", "streaming_fp32_lanes": 16, "capabilities": ["cpu", "arm64", "sme", "sme2", "neon", "simd", "single-thread"], "sme2": true, "p_core_l1d_bytes": 131072, "e_core_l1d_bytes": 65536, "cache_line_bytes": 128}, "host": {"timestamp_utc": "2026-09-25T19:11:12.511744+00:00", "battery": "Now drawing from 'AC Power'\n -InternalBattery-0 (id=21889123)\t25%; charging; (no estimate) present: true\n", "power_settings": "Battery Power:\n powermode            1\n Sleep On Power Button 1\n standby              1\n ttyskeepawake        1\n hibernatemode        3\n powernap             0\n hibernatefile        /var/vm/sleepimage\n displaysleep         10\n womp                 0\n networkoversleep     0\n sleep                3\n tcpkeepalive         1\n lessbright           1\n disksleep            10\nAC Power:\n Sleep On Power Button 1\n powermode            0\n standby              1\n ttyskeepawake        1\n hibernatemode        3\n powernap             1\n hibernatefile        /var/vm/sleepimage\n displaysleep         10\n womp                 1\n networkoversleep     0\n sleep                5\n tcpkeepalive         1\n disksleep            10\n", "thermal": "Note: No thermal warning level has been recorded\nNote: No performance warning level has been recorded\nNote: No CPU power status has been recorded\n"}, "status": "completed", "attempts": [{"experiment_id": "n512_fast_path", "status": "abstained", "reason": "The selected conversion is an identity copy: i+j*512 equals j*512+i, so it leaves A in its original layout. With params[4]=B and params[10]=that copy, sera_libxsmm_tb computes row-major A^T@B instead of A@B for general inputs. The verified mapping requires a_col_mk[i+j*512] = A[i*512+j], or the supplied sme_transpose(512, A, a_col_mk). The stated formula and required transpose conflict. Stop pending correction of the selected specification. No edits, tools, tests, or measurements were performed; no performance claim is made."}, {"experiment_id": "assembly_audit", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-n512-tb-with-timed-sme-a-transpose", "hypothesis": "Implement the selected TRANS_B descriptor and physical A transpose using the supplied sme_transpose and sera_libxsmm_tb. The conversion writes at[k*512+i]=A[i*512+k] into a fresh 1 MiB FP32 buffer. Slots [4]=B, [10]=at and [16]=C preserve row-major C=A@B. Correction to the recommendation: the supplied TB path skips generated B-stack packing and does not add A-stack packing. This tests whether the complete changed path offsets allocation, conversion, cleanup and different memory access costs; the net performance effect is unknown. Other sizes retain the existing general fallback; allocation failure calls unchanged full512 NN. All assembly and complete BSD notices remain unchanged. This descriptor-and-layout change is absent from the supplied measured history and differs from the prior C SME compute path. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, fresh-input correctness, full overwrite, tolerance 0.002, tails, n<=0 and allocation-failure checks remain required. Measure ten validation reports and ten fresh alternating paired controls on unchanged AC Automatic, preserving best-of-three timing. Report spread and comparisons against historical AC peak 1685.6230608449698 and fresh same-mode peak; retain Battery Automatic history separately. Adoption requires min(candidate)>1.05*max(paired controls) and the unchanged held-out check. No gain, causal effect or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "b675c9702c7fe13049d35a15b7e432519b44c69bfe523f0eaebabbb628b6ec9b"}, {"experiment_id": "cache_conflict_layout", "status": "failed", "error_type": "TimeoutExpired"}, {"experiment_id": "sme_fp32_tiles", "status": "abstained", "reason": "The selected store order already exists in the supplied NN baseline. After each K loop, Llibxsmm_478 and Llibxsmm_70c, the code extracts ZA0 and ZA1 and stores their outputs before extracting and storing ZA2 and ZA3. This is an alias of the measured baseline, not a distinct source change. The recommendation also misstates the tile dimensions: at 16 FP32 lanes, four ZA.S tiles hold 32\u00d732 outputs. ZA0/ZA1 cover its first 16 rows; ZA2/ZA3 cover its next 16 rows. The latter stores use x9=C_tile+32768 bytes, equal to 16 row strides. The second compute block starts at C_tile+65536 bytes, or 32 rows. Each column-panel advance is 128 bytes, or 32 columns, so the existing traversal processes 64\u00d732 blocks, not 64\u00d764. Implementing a different traversal would replace the selected experiment. No edits, tools, tests or measurements were performed. Retain the unchanged NN incumbent; no performance gain or goal completion is established."}], "trials": [{"name": "libxsmm-reference-with-unused-transpose-primitives", "hypothesis": "Original full512 NN GEMM with optional unused verified panel and transpose primitives", "source_hash": "67da75dd729b153a2129f8b1a71dd77b4d01609a94b6d2909ae69d99974fbdae", "status": "passed", "scores": [1615.8643052584557, 1672.49505540513, 1588.3754202583964, 1524.119089470969, 1684.3008396155346, 1680.7785021474074, 1591.1151005110626, 1561.0524140507628, 1676.4117832026564, 1680.34720494905], "control_scores": [], "promoted": null, "adjudication": null}, {"name": "libxsmm-n512-tb-with-timed-sme-a-transpose", "hypothesis": "Implement the selected TRANS_B descriptor and physical A transpose using the supplied sme_transpose and sera_libxsmm_tb. The conversion writes at[k*512+i]=A[i*512+k] into a fresh 1 MiB FP32 buffer. Slots [4]=B, [10]=at and [16]=C preserve row-major C=A@B. Correction to the recommendation: the supplied TB path skips generated B-stack packing and does not add A-stack packing. This tests whether the complete changed path offsets allocation, conversion, cleanup and different memory access costs; the net performance effect is unknown. Other sizes retain the existing general fallback; allocation failure calls unchanged full512 NN. All assembly and complete BSD notices remain unchanged. This descriptor-and-layout change is absent from the supplied measured history and differs from the prior C SME compute path. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, fresh-input correctness, full overwrite, tolerance 0.002, tails, n<=0 and allocation-failure checks remain required. Measure ten validation reports and ten fresh alternating paired controls on unchanged AC Automatic, preserving best-of-three timing. Report spread and comparisons against historical AC peak 1685.6230608449698 and fresh same-mode peak; retain Battery Automatic history separately. Adoption requires min(candidate)>1.05*max(paired controls) and the unchanged held-out check. No gain, causal effect or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "b675c9702c7fe13049d35a15b7e432519b44c69bfe523f0eaebabbb628b6ec9b", "status": "passed", "scores": [1484.7832814728843, 1511.605572713199, 1505.594501276598, 1433.2534226973362, 1556.1475364839325, 1045.00418379716, 1519.4430850179656, 1465.5230714609954, 1374.533810983782, 1497.8904496981363], "control_scores": [1649.7886666889258, 1532.8220648430495, 1666.441942497294, 1687.3925479742732, 1519.8043690190539, 1203.9678607007777, 1526.285460438694, 1548.2939425429986, 1343.5745678359467, 1223.8717194338858], "promoted": false, "adjudication": {"decision": "reject", "reason": "Recorded correctness passed, but eligible=false and promoted=false prohibit adoption. Across ten reports, candidate throughput was 1045.00\u20131556.15 GFLOP/s versus paired controls of 1203.97\u20131687.39. Repeat spreads were 511.14 and 483.42 GFLOP/s; the candidate won only 3/10 pairs. Its minimum, 1045.00, fails the required >1771.76 GFLOP/s threshold (1.05 \u00d7 maximum paired control). It exceeded the historical AC peak of 1685.6231, fresh baseline peak of 1684.3008, and fresh paired-control peak of 1687.3925 in 0/10 runs each. It also exceeded the separate historical Battery Automatic peak in 0/10 runs. The consistency goal is unmet under either comparator policy. No held-out result is supplied. Discard this candidate and retain the unchanged NN incumbent. These results establish no repeatable gain and do not isolate transpose, allocation, packing, or memory-access effects. Preserve the swarm-ranked queue; do not repeat this source under another name. The legacy 1800 setting does not determine this decision."}}]}, {"phase": "cpu-libxsmm-compiler-board-2026-09-25", "calls": 73, "implementations": 5, "profile": {"cpu": "Apple M4 Pro", "power": "Battery Power", "streaming_fp32_lanes": 16, "capabilities": ["cpu", "arm64", "sme", "sme2", "neon", "simd", "single-thread"], "sme2": true, "p_core_l1d_bytes": 131072, "e_core_l1d_bytes": 65536, "cache_line_bytes": 128}, "host": {"timestamp_utc": "2026-09-25T20:26:34.042428+00:00", "battery": "Now drawing from 'Battery Power'\n -InternalBattery-0 (id=21889123)\t81%; discharging; 3:12 remaining present: true\n", "power_settings": "Battery Power:\n powermode            1\n Sleep On Power Button 1\n standby              1\n ttyskeepawake        1\n hibernatemode        3\n powernap             0\n hibernatefile        /var/vm/sleepimage\n displaysleep         10\n womp                 0\n networkoversleep     0\n sleep                3\n tcpkeepalive         1\n lessbright           1\n disksleep            10\nAC Power:\n Sleep On Power Button 1\n powermode            0\n standby              1\n ttyskeepawake        1\n hibernatemode        3\n powernap             1\n hibernatefile        /var/vm/sleepimage\n displaysleep         10\n womp                 1\n networkoversleep     0\n sleep                5\n tcpkeepalive         1\n disksleep            10\n", "thermal": "Note: No thermal warning level has been recorded\nNote: No performance warning level has been recorded\nNote: No CPU power status has been recorded\n"}, "status": "failed", "attempts": [{"experiment_id": "a_transpose", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-n512-tb-with-timed-neon-a-transpose", "hypothesis": "Implement the swarm-selected conversion change: replace only the n=512 TB wrapper's SME transpose with NEON 4x4 FP32 microtiles inside 32x32 tiles. Four row loads, register transposes, and four contiguous stores produce at[k*512+i]=A[i*512+k]. Slots [4]=original B, [10]=at, and [16]=original C remain unchanged. This differs from the measured SME-transpose TB source. The hypothesis is lower conversion cost; the complete timed performance effect is unknown. NEON conversion can regress, and prior TB measurements do not isolate conversion cost. Allocation, conversion, dispatch, and free remain inside gemm. Allocation failure retains NN; other sizes retain the existing fallback. All assembly, FP32 accumulation, ABI, thread count, compiler flags, tolerance, and complete BSD notices remain unchanged. No tools or tests were run. Require compilation and correctness checks for fresh inputs, full overwrite, unchanged inputs, general sizes, tails, n<=0, and allocation failure. Measure ten reports and ten fresh alternating NN paired controls with power source and settings unchanged, preserving best-of-three timing. Report spread and comparisons against fresh same-mode peaks and the historical AC Automatic peak 1685.6230608449698; retain the Battery Automatic peak 1668.5964359101147 as separate historical context. Comparator policy remains pending. Adoption requires min(candidate)>1.05*max(paired controls) and the unchanged held-out check. No speedup or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "8d0f6fa6445416d0eda41ae5f6e2b06c0d836d1d68de52259ea0e40c6ab203fb"}, {"experiment_id": "assembly_audit", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-full512-four-step-k-loop-unroll", "hypothesis": "Implement the swarm-selected four-step unroll in Llibxsmm_478 and Llibxsmm_70c. Each group repeats the existing two loads, two pointer advances and four FP32 FMOPAs four times, then decrements X8 by four. Both counters start at 512, so each loop executes 128 groups and preserves all 512 updates in the original accumulation order. No cleanup is needed: these loops serve only the fixed full512 primitive; other sizes retain the unchanged fallback. Parameter mapping remains [4]=original B, [10]=original A, [16]=original C, with unchanged internal packing. This differs from the historical two-step unroll. Fewer loop-control instructions may improve throughput, but larger code and scheduling pressure may cause a regression. The measured effect is unknown. ABI, thread count, compiler flags, tolerance, stores, SME transitions, allocation-failure behavior and complete BSD notices remain unchanged. No tools or tests were run. Compilation and correctness validation remain required, including fresh inputs, input preservation, full overwrite, general sizes, tails and n<=0. Measure ten reports and ten fresh alternating paired controls with unchanged power source/settings and best-of-three timing. Report spread and comparisons against historical peaks and fresh same-mode peaks separately, without choosing comparator policy. Adoption requires min(candidate)>1.05*max(paired controls) and the unchanged held-out check. No speedup, causal attribution or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "d91b41bd7bbe47c6630c8f3e4e6720904acd27814cbf4e24fc7834b1938d38ac"}, {"experiment_id": "cache_conflict_layout", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-full512-padded-288-byte-a-slices", "hypothesis": "Implement only the swarm-selected 288-byte packed-A K-slice layout in the unchanged NN baseline. Allocate 147456 bytes and pack 512 slices, each containing 256 data bytes followed by 32 unused bytes. Both scratch consumers advance by 288 bytes and rewind by 147456 bytes. The second row half remains at offset 128; the final data byte is at offset 147423, within the allocation. Parameter slots remain [4]=original B, [10]=original A, [16]=original C. This differs from the measured 272-byte layout. The hypothesis is that a different scratch address pattern changes cache conflicts; cache-set geometry and performance benefit are unverified. The extra 16 KiB can cause a regression. FP32 accumulation order, input preservation, output stores, SME transitions, general-size fallback, allocation-failure behavior, ABI and complete BSD notices remain unchanged. All packing remains inside the timed gemm call. No tools or tests were run. Require compilation and correctness checks at tolerance 0.002, including both row halves, fresh inputs, full overwrite, general sizes, tails and n<=0. Measure ten validation reports and ten fresh alternating paired controls with the initial power source and settings unchanged, preserving best-of-three timing. Report spread and comparisons against fresh same-mode peaks and the historical AC Automatic peak 1685.6230608449698; retain Battery Automatic peak 1668.5964359101147 separately. Comparator policy remains pending. Adoption requires min(candidate)>1.05*max(paired controls) and the unchanged held-out check. No speedup, causal effect or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "f31c0016cb2bfafd9203b633ecd4268f3be3dd9c59e0f101bcb9ed9af6078ee4"}, {"experiment_id": "n512_fast_path", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-n512-ta-with-timed-sme-b-transpose", "hypothesis": "Implement only the swarm-selected TA full-call wrapper. The supplied sme_transpose writes bt[k*512+j]=B[j*512+k] into a fresh 1 MiB FP32 buffer inside gemm. Parameter slots are [4]=bt, [10]=original A and [16]=original C; all other slots remain zero. TA retains generated B-stack packing and adds generated A-stack packing. Its different packing and memory access pattern may improve total time, but allocation, conversion and cleanup can outweigh that effect. Performance is unknown. This wrapper is absent from the supplied measured history; the measured TB wrappers do not measure TA. Allocation failure calls unchanged NN with original inputs; n!=512 retains the existing fallback. All assembly, complete BSD notices, ABI, FP32 arithmetic, thread count, compiler flags and tolerance remain unchanged. No tools or tests were run. Require compilation and correctness checks for fresh inputs, full overwrite, input preservation, general sizes, tails, n<=0 and allocation failure at tolerance 0.002. Then collect ten validation reports and ten fresh alternating paired controls with power source and settings unchanged, preserving best-of-three timing. Report spread and comparisons against fresh same-mode peaks and historical AC Automatic peak 1685.6230608449698; keep historical Battery Automatic peak 1668.5964359101147 separate. Comparator policy remains pending. Adoption requires min(candidate)>1.05*max(paired controls) and the unchanged held-out check. No speedup, causal effect or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "6e229a14f522dcece739b3cf7feaefa1a924de3619c73629c24972ac32688b21"}, {"experiment_id": "a_transpose", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-general-size-sme-direct-a-gather", "hypothesis": "Implement the selected general-size path with direct row-major A gathers. For each 2VL-by-2VL output tile and K step, gather A[(i+lane)*n+k], load contiguous B[k*n+j+lane], and perform the existing four FP32 outer products. Predicates cover row and column tails. A guarded scalar path handles dimensions that exceed the gather index range or safe signed tile increments. The general path no longer allocates or materializes a transpose. The n=512 wrapper still calls unchanged NN with [4]=B, [10]=A and [16]=C. This change is absent from the supplied measured history. Avoiding conversion and allocation may reduce general-size call cost; repeated strided gathers may increase it. The effect is unverified. Frozen n=512 timing does not measure the new gather path, although compiler layout can change. All generated assembly and complete BSD notices remain unchanged. No tools, compilation, tests or measurements were performed. Validate fresh inputs, input preservation, full overwrite, tolerance 0.002, sizes around vector and tile boundaries, odd tails, n<=0 and the large-dimension guard. Retain ten n=512 validation reports and ten fresh alternating paired controls, best-of-three timing, unchanged power settings, separate historical and fresh same-mode comparisons, the fixed promotion gate and held-out check. No gain or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "80316af82b4447ecf4c115107301f17362174f005361dd285145ae9055dbc6d1"}], "trials": [{"name": "libxsmm-reference-with-unused-transpose-primitives", "hypothesis": "Original full512 NN GEMM with optional unused verified panel and transpose primitives", "source_hash": "67da75dd729b153a2129f8b1a71dd77b4d01609a94b6d2909ae69d99974fbdae", "status": "passed", "scores": [1001.778107426596, 1041.4566748808284, 1113.4565675720366, 1105.2411923367176, 1056.832509443394, 1088.9876521071883, 1091.7558167392897, 1012.1695265480519, 1055.967758831727, 1101.6533135285138], "control_scores": [], "promoted": null, "adjudication": null}, {"name": "libxsmm-n512-tb-with-timed-sme-a-transpose", "hypothesis": "Implement the selected TRANS_B descriptor and physical A transpose using the supplied sme_transpose and sera_libxsmm_tb. The conversion writes at[k*512+i]=A[i*512+k] into a fresh 1 MiB FP32 buffer. Slots [4]=B, [10]=at and [16]=C preserve row-major C=A@B. Correction to the recommendation: the supplied TB path skips generated B-stack packing and does not add A-stack packing. This tests whether the complete changed path offsets allocation, conversion, cleanup and different memory access costs; the net performance effect is unknown. Other sizes retain the existing general fallback; allocation failure calls unchanged full512 NN. All assembly and complete BSD notices remain unchanged. This descriptor-and-layout change is absent from the supplied measured history and differs from the prior C SME compute path. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, fresh-input correctness, full overwrite, tolerance 0.002, tails, n<=0 and allocation-failure checks remain required. Measure ten validation reports and ten fresh alternating paired controls on unchanged AC Automatic, preserving best-of-three timing. Report spread and comparisons against historical AC peak 1685.6230608449698 and fresh same-mode peak; retain Battery Automatic history separately. Adoption requires min(candidate)>1.05*max(paired controls) and the unchanged held-out check. No gain, causal effect or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "b675c9702c7fe13049d35a15b7e432519b44c69bfe523f0eaebabbb628b6ec9b", "status": "passed", "scores": [1069.996818080416, 911.7525768456192, 808.9474448189305, 992.2135982917764, 625.5414159877457, 844.8007953295727, 736.1959772224084, 1046.874849004045, 1004.2779488006342, 1013.4420458918961], "control_scores": [1045.8510638953478, 1090.2791739550196, 984.332901433359, 1096.585911223374, 1096.5903440043105, 1066.9856778717942, 1037.0950363016157, 1076.7912840343354, 993.5908848909261, 1106.1884974295049], "promoted": false, "adjudication": {"decision": "reject", "reason": "Recorded correctness passed, but eligible=false and promoted=false prohibit adoption. Across ten reports, candidate scores were 625.54\u20131070.00 GFLOP/s versus paired controls of 984.33\u20131106.19. Repeat spreads were 444.46 and 121.86 GFLOP/s. The candidate won only 2/10 pairs. Its minimum of 625.54 fails the required >1161.50 GFLOP/s threshold (1.05 \u00d7 maximum paired control). It exceeded the fresh baseline peak of 1113.46 and paired-control peak of 1106.19 in 0/10 reports. It also exceeded the historical AC Automatic peak of 1685.6231 and separate Battery Automatic peak of 1668.5964 in 0/10 reports each. Neither comparator establishes goal completion; comparator policy remains pending. No held-out result is supplied. Discard this TB wrapper and retain the unchanged NN incumbent. Preserve this replay separately from prior AC measurements. These results do not isolate transpose, allocation, packing or compute costs. TA and TT full-call wrappers remain unmeasured. Preserve the swarm-ranked queue and fixed gates; the legacy 1800 setting does not determine this decision."}}, {"name": "libxsmm-n512-tb-with-timed-neon-a-transpose", "hypothesis": "Implement the swarm-selected conversion change: replace only the n=512 TB wrapper's SME transpose with NEON 4x4 FP32 microtiles inside 32x32 tiles. Four row loads, register transposes, and four contiguous stores produce at[k*512+i]=A[i*512+k]. Slots [4]=original B, [10]=at, and [16]=original C remain unchanged. This differs from the measured SME-transpose TB source. The hypothesis is lower conversion cost; the complete timed performance effect is unknown. NEON conversion can regress, and prior TB measurements do not isolate conversion cost. Allocation, conversion, dispatch, and free remain inside gemm. Allocation failure retains NN; other sizes retain the existing fallback. All assembly, FP32 accumulation, ABI, thread count, compiler flags, tolerance, and complete BSD notices remain unchanged. No tools or tests were run. Require compilation and correctness checks for fresh inputs, full overwrite, unchanged inputs, general sizes, tails, n<=0, and allocation failure. Measure ten reports and ten fresh alternating NN paired controls with power source and settings unchanged, preserving best-of-three timing. Report spread and comparisons against fresh same-mode peaks and the historical AC Automatic peak 1685.6230608449698; retain the Battery Automatic peak 1668.5964359101147 as separate historical context. Comparator policy remains pending. Adoption requires min(candidate)>1.05*max(paired controls) and the unchanged held-out check. No speedup or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "8d0f6fa6445416d0eda41ae5f6e2b06c0d836d1d68de52259ea0e40c6ab203fb", "status": "passed", "scores": [924.8422313533212, 600.0233700329317, 683.6211184714585, 764.7733895179424, 690.1399594114687, 962.8555116118192, 883.0113653669279, 959.8396256094588, 696.1049158930257, 784.3256537789443], "control_scores": [983.1287748527419, 1076.2516886107835, 1093.4234161298493, 1063.637266332398, 945.1952382091855, 1011.8528394233884, 810.5742886113172, 800.8026315463463, 1025.8666960805672, 1016.1581732822739], "promoted": false, "adjudication": {"decision": "reject", "reason": "Recorded correctness passed, but eligible=false and promoted=false prohibit adoption. Across ten reports, this NEON-transpose TB candidate scored 600.02\u2013962.86 GFLOP/s versus paired NN controls of 800.80\u20131093.42. Repeat spreads were 362.83 and 292.62 GFLOP/s; the candidate won only 2/10 pairs. Its minimum of 600.02 fails the required >1148.09 GFLOP/s threshold (1.05 \u00d7 maximum paired control).\n\nIt exceeded the fresh baseline peak of 1113.46 and fresh paired-control peak of 1093.42 in 0/10 reports each. It also exceeded the historical AC Automatic peak of 1685.6231 and separate Battery Automatic peak of 1668.5964 in 0/10 reports each. The ten-run goal is unmet under either comparator policy. No held-out result is supplied.\n\nDiscard this candidate and retain the unchanged NN incumbent. These results establish no repeatable gain and do not isolate conversion, allocation, compute, or cache costs, or establish NEON versus SME transpose performance. Keep power-mode records separate. TA and TT full-call wrappers remain unmeasured. Preserve the swarm-ranked queue and fixed gates; the legacy 1800 setting does not determine this decision."}}, {"name": "libxsmm-full512-four-step-k-loop-unroll", "hypothesis": "Implement the swarm-selected four-step unroll in Llibxsmm_478 and Llibxsmm_70c. Each group repeats the existing two loads, two pointer advances and four FP32 FMOPAs four times, then decrements X8 by four. Both counters start at 512, so each loop executes 128 groups and preserves all 512 updates in the original accumulation order. No cleanup is needed: these loops serve only the fixed full512 primitive; other sizes retain the unchanged fallback. Parameter mapping remains [4]=original B, [10]=original A, [16]=original C, with unchanged internal packing. This differs from the historical two-step unroll. Fewer loop-control instructions may improve throughput, but larger code and scheduling pressure may cause a regression. The measured effect is unknown. ABI, thread count, compiler flags, tolerance, stores, SME transitions, allocation-failure behavior and complete BSD notices remain unchanged. No tools or tests were run. Compilation and correctness validation remain required, including fresh inputs, input preservation, full overwrite, general sizes, tails and n<=0. Measure ten reports and ten fresh alternating paired controls with unchanged power source/settings and best-of-three timing. Report spread and comparisons against historical peaks and fresh same-mode peaks separately, without choosing comparator policy. Adoption requires min(candidate)>1.05*max(paired controls) and the unchanged held-out check. No speedup, causal attribution or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "d91b41bd7bbe47c6630c8f3e4e6720904acd27814cbf4e24fc7834b1938d38ac", "status": "passed", "scores": [1047.2097393565439, 792.9185793544706, 1034.9318947191177, 994.2053775205765, 1090.2791739550196, 800.4038771425506, 935.5890270022921, 825.1098483801958, 1102.404309429142, 1040.447503752028], "control_scores": [1034.5968021956367, 1040.1128771679143, 969.8092704952953, 992.0632800545, 1083.130403247496, 997.4378395278604, 1057.0030978642221, 822.8940754065302, 934.0946530838439, 868.8412573259095], "promoted": false, "adjudication": {"decision": "reject", "reason": "Recorded correctness passed, but eligible=false and promoted=false prohibit adoption. Across ten reports, the four-step unroll scored 792.92\u20131102.40 GFLOP/s versus paired controls of 822.89\u20131083.13. Repeat spreads were 309.49 and 260.24 GFLOP/s. It won 7/10 pairs, but the overlapping ranges establish no consistent gain. Its minimum of 792.92 fails the required >1137.29 GFLOP/s threshold (1.05 \u00d7 maximum paired control).\n\nIt exceeded the fresh baseline peak of 1113.46 in 0/10 reports and its paired-control peak of 1083.13 in 2/10. It exceeded the historical AC Automatic peak of 1685.6231 and separate Battery Automatic peak of 1668.5964 in 0/10 each. The ten-run goal is unmet under either comparator policy. No held-out result is supplied.\n\nDiscard this candidate and retain the unchanged NN incumbent. These measurements establish no causal benefit from reduced loop control. Preserve separate power-mode records, the swarm-ranked queue, and fixed gates. Do not repeat this source under another name. The legacy 1800 setting does not determine this decision."}}, {"name": "libxsmm-full512-padded-288-byte-a-slices", "hypothesis": "Implement only the swarm-selected 288-byte packed-A K-slice layout in the unchanged NN baseline. Allocate 147456 bytes and pack 512 slices, each containing 256 data bytes followed by 32 unused bytes. Both scratch consumers advance by 288 bytes and rewind by 147456 bytes. The second row half remains at offset 128; the final data byte is at offset 147423, within the allocation. Parameter slots remain [4]=original B, [10]=original A, [16]=original C. This differs from the measured 272-byte layout. The hypothesis is that a different scratch address pattern changes cache conflicts; cache-set geometry and performance benefit are unverified. The extra 16 KiB can cause a regression. FP32 accumulation order, input preservation, output stores, SME transitions, general-size fallback, allocation-failure behavior, ABI and complete BSD notices remain unchanged. All packing remains inside the timed gemm call. No tools or tests were run. Require compilation and correctness checks at tolerance 0.002, including both row halves, fresh inputs, full overwrite, general sizes, tails and n<=0. Measure ten validation reports and ten fresh alternating paired controls with the initial power source and settings unchanged, preserving best-of-three timing. Report spread and comparisons against fresh same-mode peaks and the historical AC Automatic peak 1685.6230608449698; retain Battery Automatic peak 1668.5964359101147 separately. Comparator policy remains pending. Adoption requires min(candidate)>1.05*max(paired controls) and the unchanged held-out check. No speedup, causal effect or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "f31c0016cb2bfafd9203b633ecd4268f3be3dd9c59e0f101bcb9ed9af6078ee4", "status": "passed", "scores": [1089.5401614676123, 915.5120612687192, 974.5023639529999, 866.6197093727466, 841.9312150732358, 1075.7125082549735, 1012.326055594333, 992.826494863708, 1094.3506278593577, 1091.019189636549], "control_scores": [1022.9386130557521, 1046.8707496332781, 810.7799261567576, 931.1234709823614, 1088.9876521071883, 973.9155264894788, 895.9047436941847, 1063.8100587822496, 969.6621465448887, 815.0882215316337], "promoted": false, "adjudication": {"decision": "reject", "reason": "Recorded correctness passed, but eligible=false and promoted=false prohibit adoption. Across ten reports, the 288-byte padding candidate scored 841.93\u20131094.35 GFLOP/s versus paired controls of 810.78\u20131088.99. Repeat spreads were 252.42 and 278.21 GFLOP/s. It won 6/10 pairs; the overlapping ranges establish no consistent gain. Its minimum of 841.93 fails the required >1143.44 GFLOP/s threshold (1.05 \u00d7 maximum paired control).\n\nIt exceeded the fresh baseline peak of 1113.46 in 0/10 reports and its paired-control peak of 1088.99 in 3/10. It exceeded the historical AC Automatic peak of 1685.6231 and separate Battery Automatic peak of 1668.5964 in 0/10 each. The ten-run goal is unmet under either comparator policy. No held-out result is supplied.\n\nDiscard this candidate and retain the unchanged NN incumbent. These results do not establish a cache-conflict cause or isolate padding costs. Preserve separate power-mode records, the swarm-ranked queue, and fixed gates. Do not repeat this source under another name. The legacy 1800 setting does not determine this decision."}}, {"name": "libxsmm-n512-ta-with-timed-sme-b-transpose", "hypothesis": "Implement only the swarm-selected TA full-call wrapper. The supplied sme_transpose writes bt[k*512+j]=B[j*512+k] into a fresh 1 MiB FP32 buffer inside gemm. Parameter slots are [4]=bt, [10]=original A and [16]=original C; all other slots remain zero. TA retains generated B-stack packing and adds generated A-stack packing. Its different packing and memory access pattern may improve total time, but allocation, conversion and cleanup can outweigh that effect. Performance is unknown. This wrapper is absent from the supplied measured history; the measured TB wrappers do not measure TA. Allocation failure calls unchanged NN with original inputs; n!=512 retains the existing fallback. All assembly, complete BSD notices, ABI, FP32 arithmetic, thread count, compiler flags and tolerance remain unchanged. No tools or tests were run. Require compilation and correctness checks for fresh inputs, full overwrite, input preservation, general sizes, tails, n<=0 and allocation failure at tolerance 0.002. Then collect ten validation reports and ten fresh alternating paired controls with power source and settings unchanged, preserving best-of-three timing. Report spread and comparisons against fresh same-mode peaks and historical AC Automatic peak 1685.6230608449698; keep historical Battery Automatic peak 1668.5964359101147 separate. Comparator policy remains pending. Adoption requires min(candidate)>1.05*max(paired controls) and the unchanged held-out check. No speedup, causal effect or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "6e229a14f522dcece739b3cf7feaefa1a924de3619c73629c24972ac32688b21", "status": "passed", "scores": [752.7993396767996, 779.6760554137518, 764.6818643320042, 727.467358011839, 769.9833668307898, 588.9429001515639, 630.3758319468445, 617.328579467292, 738.1353145091299, 785.185980977845], "control_scores": [1043.8217155677105, 1007.7351491779309, 993.745360286824, 795.2653345687437, 992.6759374591788, 1105.8103218973295, 1051.6569926816014, 1059.7907376158284, 1051.3151780119256, 976.7184966167833], "promoted": false, "adjudication": {"decision": "reject", "reason": "Recorded correctness passed, but eligible=false and promoted=false prohibit adoption. Across ten reports, this TA wrapper scored 588.94\u2013785.19 GFLOP/s versus paired NN controls of 795.27\u20131105.81. Repeat spreads were 196.24 and 310.54 GFLOP/s. It lost all ten pairs; even its maximum was below the minimum control. Its minimum of 588.94 fails the required >1161.10 GFLOP/s threshold (1.05 \u00d7 maximum paired control).\n\nIt exceeded the fresh baseline peak of 1113.46, paired-control peak of 1105.81, historical AC Automatic peak of 1685.6231, and separate Battery Automatic peak of 1668.5964 in 0/10 reports each. The ten-run goal is unmet under either comparator policy. No held-out result is supplied.\n\nDiscard this candidate and retain the unchanged NN incumbent. This complete TA wrapper is now measured; TT remains unmeasured. These results do not isolate transpose, allocation, internal packing, or compute costs. Preserve separate power-mode records, the swarm-ranked queue, and fixed gates. The legacy 1800 setting does not determine this decision."}}, {"name": "libxsmm-general-size-sme-direct-a-gather", "hypothesis": "Implement the selected general-size path with direct row-major A gathers. For each 2VL-by-2VL output tile and K step, gather A[(i+lane)*n+k], load contiguous B[k*n+j+lane], and perform the existing four FP32 outer products. Predicates cover row and column tails. A guarded scalar path handles dimensions that exceed the gather index range or safe signed tile increments. The general path no longer allocates or materializes a transpose. The n=512 wrapper still calls unchanged NN with [4]=B, [10]=A and [16]=C. This change is absent from the supplied measured history. Avoiding conversion and allocation may reduce general-size call cost; repeated strided gathers may increase it. The effect is unverified. Frozen n=512 timing does not measure the new gather path, although compiler layout can change. All generated assembly and complete BSD notices remain unchanged. No tools, compilation, tests or measurements were performed. Validate fresh inputs, input preservation, full overwrite, tolerance 0.002, sizes around vector and tile boundaries, odd tails, n<=0 and the large-dimension guard. Retain ten n=512 validation reports and ten fresh alternating paired controls, best-of-three timing, unchanged power settings, separate historical and fresh same-mode comparisons, the fixed promotion gate and held-out check. No gain or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "80316af82b4447ecf4c115107301f17362174f005361dd285145ae9055dbc6d1", "status": "rejected", "scores": [], "control_scores": [], "promoted": false, "adjudication": null}]}, {"phase": "cpu-libxsmm-strassen-swarm-2026-09-25", "calls": 71, "implementations": 6, "profile": {"cpu": "Apple M4 Pro", "power": "Battery Power", "streaming_fp32_lanes": 16, "capabilities": ["cpu", "arm64", "sme", "sme2", "neon", "simd", "single-thread"], "sme2": true, "p_core_l1d_bytes": 131072, "e_core_l1d_bytes": 65536, "cache_line_bytes": 128}, "host": {"timestamp_utc": "2026-09-25T21:09:11.789525+00:00", "battery": "Now drawing from 'Battery Power'\n -InternalBattery-0 (id=21889123)\t67%; discharging; 2:46 remaining present: true\n", "power_settings": "Battery Power:\n powermode            1\n Sleep On Power Button 1\n standby              1\n ttyskeepawake        1\n hibernatemode        3\n powernap             0\n hibernatefile        /var/vm/sleepimage\n displaysleep         10\n womp                 0\n networkoversleep     0\n sleep                3\n tcpkeepalive         1\n lessbright           1\n disksleep            10\nAC Power:\n Sleep On Power Button 1\n powermode            0\n standby              1\n ttyskeepawake        1\n hibernatemode        3\n powernap             1\n hibernatefile        /var/vm/sleepimage\n displaysleep         10\n womp                 1\n networkoversleep     0\n sleep                5\n tcpkeepalive         1\n disksleep            10\n", "thermal": "Note: No thermal warning level has been recorded\nNote: No performance warning level has been recorded\nNote: No CPU power status has been recorded\n"}, "status": "final-performance-unconfirmed", "attempts": [{"experiment_id": "strassen_one_level", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-n512-one-level-strassen-three-buffers", "hypothesis": "Implement the supplied swarm-selected schedule: seven dense 256-square products, three reusable FP32 buffers, and signed accumulation into zeroed stride512 output quadrants. Each helper call uses a fresh zeroed parameter array with [4]=right, [10]=left and [16]=product. All allocations, quadrant copies, sums, helper calls, recombination and frees execute within gemm. Allocation failure and n!=512 use the unchanged general fallback. Imported assembly and all BSD notices remain unchanged. This wrapper is absent from the supplied measured history. Reduced multiplication count does not establish a runtime gain; copying, allocation, transitions and recombination can erase it. FP32 cancellation and scale-separated accuracy remain unverified. No tools, compilation, tests or measurements were performed. Require the complete correctness checks, including tolerance 0.002, finite output, input preservation, full overwrite, output guards, allocation failure, general sizes, tails and n<=0, before timing. Then require ten validations and ten alternating paired controls with unchanged power settings, followed by the fixed min(candidate)>1.05*max(control) gate and held-out checking. The supplied fresh battery baseline spans 905.47\u20131102.21 GFLOP/s, with peak 1102.214208818538; no candidate or paired-control results exist for this wrapper. Keep historical Battery Automatic peak 1668.5964359101147, AC initial-baseline peak 1685.6230608449698 and later AC unchanged-control peak 1687.3925479742732 separate from fresh same-mode results. Comparator policy remains pending. No speedup, causal attribution or goal completion is established.", "source_hash": "ec4b06039d12d06ab3475c871c3a898aee6cb971be8d781f29b7a5d688c5d8f1"}, {"experiment_id": "cache_blocking", "status": "abstained", "reason": "Stop: the selected workspace schedule was already measured as libxsmm-n512-one-level-strassen-three-buffers, source ec4b06039d12d06ab3475c871c3a898aee6cb971be8d781f29b7a5d688c5d8f1. It already uses three reusable dense buffers, seven approved products, immediate signed recombination and one initial C zeroing. Correctness passed, but it lost all ten pairs: 432.96\u2013567.57 GFLOP/s versus controls of 776.29\u20131091.57, and was rejected. Changing only allocation-failure dispatch from the general fallback to full512 NN does not create a distinct workspace experiment. No edits, tools, tests or new measurements were performed."}, {"experiment_id": "panel_packing", "status": "abstained", "reason": "Cannot implement the selected layout as specified. A dense 32-row panel across K=512 requires 512*32*4 = 65536 bytes (64 KiB), twice the requested 32 KiB. The specified packed_a[k*32+r] accesses float index 16383, beyond a 32 KiB allocation. A 32 KiB buffer would require changing the panel dimensions or splitting K, which changes the selected experiment. The prior measured one-SME-region panel32 candidate already uses a 64 KiB buffer and sixteen 32-row bands; it failed promotion. No substitute, source edits, tests or measurements were performed."}, {"experiment_id": "cache_blocking", "status": "abstained", "reason": "Stop: the selected experiment repeats libxsmm-n512-panel32-one-streaming-region, source eb091b1eca431f0760d0d61e4c0c6e748c1a9e34466a87ac15ad9cb238b5aecf. That measured implementation already packs sixteen 32-row bands into one reusable 64 KiB scratch buffer, computes all sixteen column panels per band, and uses one SME region for the full call. The claim that this structure is unmeasured contradicts the supplied history. Moving the same schedule into the full512 body does not define a new experiment.\n\nRecorded correctness passed, but promotion failed on Battery Low Power and AC Automatic. Across ten AC runs, candidate scores were 1251.20\u20131701.65 GFLOP/s versus paired controls of 1225.26\u20131673.37; only 5/10 pairs improved. It exceeded the historical Battery Automatic peak 1668.5964 in 3/10 runs and that block's fresh AC baseline peak 1685.6231 in 1/10. The later historical AC unchanged-control peak is 1687.3925. The current prepared battery baseline peak is 1102.2142; no new candidate or paired-control measurements were made. Keep power modes separate. No causal benefit or goal completion is established. No edits, tools or tests were performed."}, {"experiment_id": "assembly_audit", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-full512-subs-bne-k-loop-control", "hypothesis": "Replace SUB/CBNZ with SUBS/B.NE in both active NN K loops. Each counter starts at 512 and exits when its decrement reaches zero, preserving all 512 ordered FP32 updates. Instruction count remains two; performance is unknown. This change is distinct from the supplied measured candidates. Loads, pointer updates, FMOPA order, rewinds, ABI, fallback, unused helpers and all BSD notices remain unchanged. No tools or tests were run. Compilation and all fixed correctness checks, including cancellation and scale-separated cases, remain required before timing. Require ten validations and ten alternating paired controls with power settings unchanged, then min(candidate)>1.05*max(control) and held-out checking. The supplied fresh battery baseline peak is 1102.214208818538 GFLOP/s; this candidate has no measurements or paired controls. Report fresh same-mode comparisons separately from historical Battery Automatic peak 1668.5964359101147, AC initial-baseline peak 1685.6230608449698 and AC unchanged-control peak 1687.3925479742732. No speedup, causal attribution or goal completion is established; comparator policy remains pending.", "source_hash": "b8dc2f35cc95da3c11ebbbf037cbee47be2d9a891849a579050006c95726f0c9"}, {"experiment_id": "vector_access", "status": "proposed", "name": "libxsmm-strassen-three-buffers-neon-packing", "hypothesis": "Replace only the measured three-buffer Strassen wrapper's packing loops with four-lane NEON FP32 loads, copies, additions, subtractions and stores. Each 256-element row uses 64 groups with no alignment assumption. Product calls, recombination, allocation, fallback and all BSD notices remain unchanged. This source change is absent from the supplied measured history. Compilation, correctness and performance are untested; the compiler may already vectorize the original loops. Require all fixed correctness checks, including cancellation, scale separation, guards and allocation failure, before ten validations and ten alternating paired controls under unchanged power settings. Promotion still requires min(candidate)>1.05*max(control), followed by held-out checking. The fresh same-mode baseline peak is 1102.214208818538 GFLOP/s; the prior Strassen wrapper's paired-control peak is 1091.5737628886607. Keep historical Battery Automatic peak 1668.5964359101147, AC initial-baseline peak 1685.6230608449698 and AC unchanged-control peak 1687.3925479742732 separate. No new measurements, speedup, causal attribution or goal completion are established.", "source_hash": "c905f5852b983554b3a6b1800f3277bc54dcb307fcd026e3efe