3.130403247496, 1063.637266332398, 917.4676523737388], "control_scores": [], "promoted": null, "adjudication": null}, {"name": "libxsmm-n512-panel32-one-streaming-region", "hypothesis": "Reuse the panel32 packing and compute body for sixteen row panels inside one SME region with one 64 KiB scratch allocation. Saved registers x21/x22/x23 retain B/A/C bases, x26 retains scratch, x27 counts panels, and x28 holds the byte offset; these registers are saved and restored by the existing prologue and epilogue and are otherwise unused by the supplied helper body. Each panel resets B, A, C, scratch and the packing cursor. A and C advance by 65536 bytes, covering all 512 output rows once. SP resets to scratch after packing and returns to the saved stack top after the last panel. The FP32 K loop, ZA setup, output stores, general-size fallback and complete license notices remain unchanged. This differs from the measured sixteen-call wrapper. Reduced entry/exit overhead is an unverified hypothesis; comparison against full512 measures the complete layout and control-flow change and cannot isolate transition costs. No tools or tests were run. Compilation, full-GEMM correctness and fresh repeated paired performance validation remain required under the unchanged gates and initial power settings. No speedup or throughput above 1800 GFLOP/s is established.", "source_hash": "eb091b1eca431f0760d0d61e4c0c6e748c1a9e34466a87ac15ad9cb238b5aecf", "status": "passed", "scores": [1106.3799715342993, 887.8771809034087, 1108.6647177394075, 714.7947585527811, 1101.6488397207727, 1037.9331701592325, 1094.7254871859825, 1085.4998855292538, 1045.00418379716, 1068.3998576668903], "control_scores": [933.4191289520478, 1027.8346679179053, 1094.7254871859825, 942.7056796829798, 1080.2231610103274, 1037.9330533575746, 1077.87222568128, 1074.4552467023284, 969.2280700219095, 1088.6210156938728], "promoted": false, "adjudication": {"decision": "revise", "reason": "Retain the incumbent unchanged; do not promote eb091b1e\u2026. Correctness passed at tolerance 0.002, but eligible=false. The fresh replay won 7/10 pairs, including one near-tie. Candidate scores ranged from 714.794759 to 1108.664718 GFLOP/s; paired controls ranged from 933.419129 to 1094.725487. These ranges overlap, so the required separated-range-plus-5% gate fails. Repeatable improvement is not established.\n\nFresh peaks were 1108.664718 for the candidate, 1094.725487 for paired controls, and 1100.524173 for the separate initial imported-control block. All ten candidate scores were below the historical Battery Automatic imported peak of 1668.5964359101147. Historical AC observations remain separate: candidate peak 1701.6509826, that phase's initial imported peak 1685.6230608, and later control peak 1687.3925479742732. The prior AC result had only 1/10 initial-peak exceedances and 5/10 paired wins; it contributes nothing to current eligibility.\n\nNo cause for variation or system-wide optimum is established. Goal policy remains pending; the legacy 1800 target does not determine success. Raw timing triplets and held-out confirmation were not supplied, so their preservation and results cannot be verified here. No new measurements, source edits, or power changes were performed."}}]}]
